.TH WERKMEISTER-UP 1 "" "werkmeister" "Werkmeister Manual"
.SH NAME
werkmeister\-up \- Detect services, allocate slot, generate config, start containers
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwerkmeister up\fR [feature]
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-w, \-\-workspace <path>\fR
Path to directory containing repo checkouts. Default: ~/workspace (override with WORKSPACE env var).
.TP
\fB\-\-dev\fR
Run the file watchers in cli/library/extension containers, which otherwise idle.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The local services come from the workspace's \fB.werkmeister/workspace.yml\fR (via \fBwerkmeister init\-workspace\fR), not from a flag.
.PP
\fBWhat it does:\fR
.IP 1. 3
Loads service registry and port configuration
.IP 2. 3
Resolves the workspace (default: \fB~/workspace/\fR) and reads its local services from the \fBSERVICES=\fR line \fBwerkmeister init\-workspace\fR wrote to the workspace \fB.env\fR
.IP 3. 3
Allocates a slot (1–12) if the feature doesn't already have one
.IP 4. 3
Generates per\-feature files in the feature's workspace:
.IP \(bu 6
\fBcompose.yml\fR — Docker Compose stack definition (workspace root)
.IP \(bu 6
\fB.env\fR — Environment variables with resolved service URLs (workspace root)
.IP \(bu 6
\fB<workspace>/.werkmeister/supergraph\-config.yml\fR — GraphQL federation config (only when a service has a GraphQL type: \fBgraphql\-subgraph\fR, \fBgraphql\fR, \fBsubgraph\fR or \fBfederation\fR)
.IP 5. 3
Verifies k8s port\-forwards are healthy (restarts if needed)
.IP 6. 3
Starts containers with \fBdocker compose up \-d \-\-build \-\-remove\-orphans\fR
.IP 7. 3
Regenerates \fB~/.werkmeister/infra/proxy/Caddyfile\fR and reloads Caddy
.PP
\fBOutput example:\fR
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
[info] Scanning workspace for feature: my\-feature
[info] Detected 2 service(s): backend, frontend
[ok]   Allocated slot 1 (ports 11100\-11119)
[info] Generating config files...
[info] Starting containers...
[ok]   Feature 'my\-feature' is up!

  URL:       https://frontend.local.werkmeister.io
  Header:    X\-Feature: my\-feature
  Slot:      1
  Ports:     11100\-11119
  Services:  backend (:11100), frontend (:11101)
.RE
.fi
.PP
\fBIf the workspace lists no services\fR, the command still proceeds — the feature is registered and routes entirely to k8s. To add services later, list them in \fB.werkmeister/workspace.yml\fR, rerun \fBwerkmeister init\-workspace\fR, then \fBwerkmeister up\fR.
.PP
\fBIf every slot is taken\fR (12 by default, \fBfeature_slots.count\fR), the command exits with an error. Free a slot by running \fBwerkmeister down\fR on another feature.
.PP
\fBAdding a service to a running feature.\fR \fBwerkmeister up\fR takes no service list. To run another service locally, add it to the \fBservices\fR field in the workspace's \fB.werkmeister/workspace.yml\fR, rerun \fBwerkmeister init\-workspace\fR (this also adds the owning repo's worktree if it isn't there yet), then \fBwerkmeister up\fR.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBwerkmeister\fR(1)
